title: Economic Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: economic_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1; 
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and (economic_minister_party == "SPD" or finance_minister_party == "SPD") and economic_policy_timer <= 0 
card-image: img/portraits/SchmidtRobert.jpg
#subtitle: Policies to address the economic crisis.

= Economic Policy

We have already formulated an economic plan. Now we have to implement it.

- @cap: Enact the Market Liberal plan of economic freedom and privatisation.
- @lib: Begin Privatisation of Minority shares of Government Companies.
- @socdem: Balance Economic Decentralisation with worker's rights and improved wages.
- @nah: Do not enact economic reforms.

@cap
choose-if: cap_strength >= 30
subtitle: The Plan primarily focuses on empowering the private sector (+2 budget).
unavailable-subtitle: The Capitalists do not have enough support.
on-arrival: cap_policy += 1; eco_policy += 1; economic_growth += 2; inflation += 1; usp_relation += 3; old_middle_spd += 3; socdem_dissent += 8; budget += 2

Many Government owned companies have been privatised, empowering the oligarchs and also easing regulations on businesses.

@lib
choose-if: lib_strength >= 30
subtitle: A balanced form of privatisation and economic liberalism (+1 budget).
unavailable-subtitle: The Liberals do not have enough support.
on-arrival: lib_policy += 1; eco_policy += 1; economic_growth += 3; inflation += 0.5; old_middle_spd += 2; new_middle_spd += 2; socdem_dissent += 3; budget += 1 

The Liberals have taken a cautious approach to privatisation and decentralisation preferring to take their time.

@socdem
choose-if: socdem_strength >= 30
subtitle: Advancement of Worker's rights alongside less government planning.
unavailable-subtitle: The Social Democrats do not have enough support 
on-arrival: cap_dissent += 8; workers_spd += 3; lib_dissent += 3; economic_growth += 1.5 ; inflation += 0.75; cps_relation += 3; socdem_policy += 1; eco_policy += 1



@nah
on-departure: economic_growth -= 0.5

The economy is fine as is. right?
